From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:14:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] zink: present to a VK_KHR_display surface, and link
 RADV on the PS4

Kopper gets a fourth kind of surface, a display (KOPPER_DISPLAY), for a
loader with no window system. The loader fills a
kopper_display_surface_create_info (sType
VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_DISPLAY_SURFACE_CREATE_INFO_KHR, a window handle that keys
the swapchain as an X11 window does, and the index of a display): a
VkDisplaySurfaceCreateInfoKHR does not fit kopper's storage, and the loader
cannot ask Vulkan which plane and mode to use. Zink picks them: the mode of
the display's native resolution with the highest refresh rate (or the
largest), a plane that can show the display, opaque alpha where the plane
has it. The swapchain is the size of the mode, as an X11 one is the
window's. zink_kopper_query_display_extent, and kopperQueryDisplayExtent in
the DRI frontend, give the loader that size before there is a surface.
Zink enables VK_KHR_display where the driver has it.

A present mode a surface does not offer falls back to FIFO, which every
surface does: a display may offer FIFO alone (the PS4's does), where an
interval of 0 asked for IMMEDIATE or MAILBOX.

On the PS4 console there is no Vulkan loader to dlopen: RADV is
libvulkan.so.1 there and exports the Vulkan API, so zink links it and takes
vkGetInstanceProcAddr and vkGetDeviceProcAddr from it (ZINK_LINK_VULKAN).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017iduBr5J43VcTC99HLCEQm
